{"id":"65d7f190fe56b39d","group":"62","path":"62/62-thm-RCA0-omega-models.md","title":"RCA0 Omega Models Are Turing Ideals","display":"thm-RCA0-omega-models — RCA0 Omega Models Are Turing Ideals","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)","book_abbrev":"62","label":"62-thm-RCA0-omega-models","aliases":["62-thm-RCA0-omega-models"],"display":"thm-RCA0-omega-models — RCA0 Omega Models Are Turing Ideals","depends_on":["[[62-df-RCA0]]","[[62-df-omega-model]]","[[62-df-turing-ideal]]"],"source":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Theorem II.1.7","source_pages":[64],"source_pdf_pages":[82]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"62"},{"key":"label","html":"62-thm-RCA0-omega-models"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62-thm-RCA0-omega-models</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-RCA0-omega-models — RCA0 Omega Models Are Turing Ideals"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5ed7a378ff9d39c6\" href=\"?note=5ed7a378ff9d39c6\" title=\"62-df-omega-model\">62-df-omega-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0efbe3f2d5d172f3\" href=\"?note=0efbe3f2d5d172f3\" title=\"62-df-turing-ideal\">62-df-turing-ideal</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source","html":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Theorem II.1.7"},{"key":"source_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>64</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>82</span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\mathbb N)\">\\(\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\mathbb N)\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RCA}_0\">\\(\\mathrm{RCA}_0\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{OmegaModelOf}\">\\(\\operatorname{OmegaModelOf}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{TIdeal}\">\\(\\mathsf{TIdeal}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5ed7a378ff9d39c6\" href=\"?note=5ed7a378ff9d39c6\" title=\"62-df-omega-model\">62-df-omega-model</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"0efbe3f2d5d172f3\" href=\"?note=0efbe3f2d5d172f3\" title=\"62-df-turing-ideal\">62-df-turing-ideal</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}RCA0\\text{-}omega\\text{-}models}\\vdash\\;\\operatorname{OmegaModelOf}(\\mathcal M_{\\mathcal S},\\mathrm{RCA}_0)\\leftrightarrow\\mathsf{TIdeal}(\\mathcal S).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}RCA0\\text{-}omega\\text{-}models}\\vdash\\;\\operatorname{OmegaModelOf}(\\mathcal M_{\\mathcal S},\\mathrm{RCA}_0)\\leftrightarrow\\mathsf{TIdeal}(\\mathcal S).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>证明依据：在标准自然数上所有归纳实例都真；Δ⁰₁ 理解恰好形成可递归于有限集合参数 join 的数集。相对递归集合及其补集均为 Σ⁰₁ 可定义（II.1.6），所以两方向分别给出向下闭包和所需理解。非空及 join 闭包处理空参数与多个参数。该刻画限定标准一阶部分，不能直接套到任意非 ω 模型。</p>\n<p>来源：第二版（2009），Theorem II.1.7；纸面页 64；PDF 页 82。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"62-df-RCA0","status":"resolved","id":"dd5e8930337c8b20","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-RCA0]]